From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] keep normal filter-pass traffic outside monitor RX

0012 completed monitor vdev channel initialization and received 27050 real
radiotap packets, but STA gateway traffic remained 1/48. Default monitor
filters include both normal filter-pass and other-BSS management/data. The
actual pinned kiwi_v2 build uses monitor 1.0 (ELF symbols and object list),
so apply to its destination and status filters, not the unused 2.0 source.
Under the default-off 0009 experiment only, disable filter-pass capture and
observe other-BSS management/data. No DMA ring ownership, firmware, TX,
channel policy or normal RX path code is changed. Verify gateway traffic
and actual monitor packets again; receiving frames alone is not coexistence.

diff --git a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_filter_1.0.c b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_filter_1.0.c
--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_filter_1.0.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_filter_1.0.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
  * OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.
